Yes, Claude is free. Anthropic runs a $0 Free plan at claude.ai, and as of November 25, 2026 it includes web search, memory, file creation with code execution, connectors, Artifacts, voice mode, up to five projects, and the Docs, Slides and Design tools. What it does not include is Opus, Claude Code, Research or scheduled tasks, and the usage allowance is small and unpublished. If you searched "cloud ai free", "cloude ai free" or "cloud ia gratis" and landed here, you probably meant Claude (the search results for those spellings mostly show cloud-platform free tiers, which we explain below), and this guide answers the Claude question with dated prices and primary sources.

The harder questions sit one layer down. How far does Free actually go before it stops you? Is there a student discount (no, but there are real free routes)? Is there a free plan for teachers (yes, in the US, through July 30, 2028)? And is it better than ChatGPT Free, Gemini's free tier or Meta's free Muse? We checked Anthropic's pricing page and help center today, plus the matching vendor pages for the rivals, and we mark what we could not confirm.

{% youtube id="4zMYK-QOv0A" title="The NEW Ultimate Beginner's Guide To Claude (September 2026)" /%}

*A third-party beginner walkthrough from the AI Edge channel, titled September 2026. We confirmed the title and channel through YouTube oEmbed but did not watch it end to end, so check any price or limit it quotes against Anthropic's pricing page, because Anthropic changes plans and limits often.*

## Short answer: what is free, what is not

- **Best free chat assistant for writing, files and tools (our pick):** Claude Free, if you can live with a small allowance and no Opus.
- **Best free plan for sheer volume of text chat:** ChatGPT Free, which OpenAI describes as unlimited everyday text chats subject to abuse safeguards, with separate caps on tools.
- **Best free plan if you live in Google apps:** Gemini free, bundled with 15 GB of Google storage and a Google Account.
- **Best free plan if you want an agent that takes actions:** Meta's Muse, free with a usage limit, but in limited testing and not available everywhere.
- **Best free route for US K-12 teachers:** Claude for Teachers, free through July 30, 2028 for verified US educators.
- **Best free route for university students:** your university's Claude for Education account, if your school has signed one. There is no student discount code.
- **Best free route for lab researchers:** the Claude Team plan for scientists, where a verified principal investigator can get $0 Standard seats for 12 months (limited availability).
- **Best paid upgrade for most people:** Claude Pro at $17 per month billed annually or $20 monthly. Skip Max until Pro actually stops you.

{% callout type="info" %}
Quick answer for the impatient: Claude Free costs $0 and needs only an email address, no card. Claude Pro is $20 a month ($17 a month if you pay $200 up front for a year). There is no standard student discount. Teachers in the US and lab groups can get free seats through separate programs. All prices are from claude.com/pricing and Anthropic's help center as of November 25, 2026, and exclude tax.
{% /callout %}

## What people mean by "cloud ai free", "cloude ai free" and "cloud ia gratis"

We ran the exact search "cloud ai free" on November 25, 2026. The top results were Google Cloud's free tier, an AI Pricing Index page of free compute deals, the AWS Free Tier, AWS's free AI services page and AIMap's list of free LLM APIs. None of them is Claude. Google Cloud's free tier is $300 in credit for new customers plus monthly free usage on specific products, and AWS offers up to $200 in credits. That is a different thing from a chat assistant.

So there are two readings of the query. If you want a chatbot like Claude without paying, this guide covers it. If you want free cloud infrastructure or free model APIs for building apps, that is a developer question: Google AI Studio, Groq, OpenRouter and Cloudflare Workers AI all publish free allowances, and one third-party tracker (AIMap, last verified November 23, 2026) lists them with limits. Claude's chat plans and the Claude API are billed separately: Anthropic's Pro help article says the Pro plan does not include API usage through the Claude Console. We did not find a Claude API free tier in the pages we read.

The Spanish search "cloud ia gratis" follows the same logic, and many people likely mean "Claude IA gratis" (our assumption, not something we measured). Anthropic has a help article on using Claude in your preferred language; we have not tested Spanish quality ourselves. A Spanish version of this guide is planned.

