## Feature matrix

| Feature | Claude Free | Claude Pro | Claude Max | ChatGPT Free | Gemini free | Meta Muse free |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Web search | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes | Not confirmed | Not confirmed |
| Memory | Yes | Yes | Yes | Not confirmed | Not confirmed | Not confirmed |
| File uploads and analysis | Yes (files and code execution) | Yes | Yes | Yes (capped) | Not confirmed | Not confirmed |
| Image generation | Not listed | Not listed | Not listed | Yes (capped) | Yes | Not confirmed |
| Docs, slides, design output | Yes | Yes | Yes | Not confirmed | Partial (Canvas) | Not confirmed |
| Skills | Yes | Yes | Yes | Not confirmed | Yes | Not confirmed |
| Connectors / apps | Yes | Yes | Yes | Not confirmed | Not confirmed | Yes (connects to other apps and services) |
| Top model tier | No Opus, no Fable | Opus; Fable with usage credits | Opus; Fable up to half your weekly limit | GPT-5.6 Luna (Think on mobile) | Gemini 4 Hydrogen | Not confirmed |
| Coding agent | No | Claude Code | Claude Code | Not confirmed | Not confirmed | Not confirmed |
| Research / Deep Research | No | Yes | Yes | Not confirmed | Yes (may be unavailable at peak) | Not confirmed |
| Scheduled tasks | No | Yes | Yes | Not confirmed | Not confirmed | Not confirmed |
| Ads | Not documented | Not documented | Not documented | May appear in some countries | Not confirmed | Not confirmed |
| Priority at busy times | No | No | Yes | Not confirmed | Not confirmed | Not confirmed |

"Not confirmed" means we did not find the answer on the vendor pages we fetched. It does not mean No. "Not listed" means the Claude pricing table has no such row.

## Head-to-head: which free plan to pick

### Claude Free vs ChatGPT Free

Pick **Claude Free** if you want files, Docs, Slides, Design, skills and connectors on a free plan, and you accept a small, unpublished allowance and no top-tier model. Pick **ChatGPT Free** if you mostly send text messages all day: OpenAI says everyday text chats are unlimited, subject to safeguards, and that tools have separate caps. ChatGPT Free also shows ads in some countries and cannot create new GPTs. Neither gives a published message count for the tools, so the better test is to run your own typical week on both.

### Claude Free vs Gemini free

Pick **Gemini free** if you want image generation, Deep Research and Gemini Live inside a Google Account, plus 15 GB of storage. Pick **Claude Free** if your work is documents, code and structured files and you value skills and connectors. Both use a rolling five-hour window with a weekly cap, and both can change limits without notice. Gemini may withhold heavy features such as Deep Research during peak demand for users without a Google AI plan.

### Claude Free vs Meta Muse free

Pick **Claude Free** for a documented feature list and wide availability. Pick **Meta Muse** if you specifically want an action-taking agent and you are in a supported country. Muse is in limited testing and Meta does not publish the free allowance, so it is the hardest of the four to plan around.

### Claude Free vs Claude Pro

Stay on **Free** if you hit no limits and need none of Opus, Claude Code, Research or scheduled tasks. Move to **Pro** when the limit message becomes a weekly annoyance, or the first time you need Claude Code or Research. Pro is at least 5x Free per 5-hour session by Anthropic's own wording, so for a regular user it is a step change. Go to **Max** only after Pro stops you repeatedly.

## Skills and MCP servers that work with these tools

Anthropic's pricing table marks Skills and Connectors as Yes on Free, and a third-party guide (Adam Digital, verified November 11, 2026) says Free users can use and make their own skills as long as code execution is on, and can add one custom connector. We could not confirm the custom connector cap from an Anthropic page today, so treat the "one" as second-hand. These catalog entries are all real pages on this site, each checked for HTTP 200 on November 25, 2026:

- [skill-creator](https://agentskills.codes/skills/skill-creator): Anthropic's guide for building new skills. The natural first stop if you want to test skills on a free account.
- [mcp-builder](https://agentskills.codes/skills/mcp-builder): a guide for building MCP servers so an LLM can reach an external service. Useful once you outgrow the connectors you already have.
- [pptx](https://agentskills.codes/skills/pptx): presentation creation, editing and analysis for .pptx files. An option when you want a file rather than Claude Slides.
- [docx](https://agentskills.codes/skills/docx): Word document creation with tracked changes and comments, for reports and assignments.
- [xlsx](https://agentskills.codes/skills/xlsx): spreadsheet creation and analysis with formulas, a good test of code execution on a free plan.
- [pdf](https://agentskills.codes/skills/pdf): extract text and tables, merge or split PDFs, and fill forms.
- [doc-coauthoring](https://agentskills.codes/skills/doc-coauthoring): a structured workflow for writing proposals and technical specs with Claude, handy for students and teachers drafting longer pieces.

Install a hosted skill into Claude Code (a paid-plan feature) with the download endpoint. The id comes from the catalog API:

```bash
curl -L https://agentskills.codes/api/skills/download/2 -o skill.zip \
  && unzip skill.zip -d ~/.claude/skills/skill-creator
```

We did not walk through the in-app skill upload screens for this guide, and menu names change, so follow Anthropic's current skills help page for the claude.ai steps. Our blog's [cost-planning guide to the Ultrafast and Pro tiers](https://agentskills.codes/blog/ultrafast-and-pro-tiers-cost-planning) is a good companion when you want to budget skill-heavy workflows across plans.

