| You are | Start with | Then | Why |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Curious, light user | Claude Free | Stay | No card, wide feature list |
| Heavy text chatter | ChatGPT Free | Claude Free as second opinion | Unlimited everyday text chat per OpenAI |
| Google Workspace user | Gemini free | Claude Free for documents | 15 GB storage, Deep Research |
| US K-12 teacher | Claude for Teachers | Free | $0 through July 30, 2028 |
| University student | Your school's Claude for Education | Claude Free | No standard student discount |
| Lab grad student or postdoc | Ask your PI about the scientists plan | Free | $0 Standard seats for 12 months |
| Developer wanting Claude Code | Pro | Max if Pro stalls | Claude Code is paid-only |
| All-day power user | Max | Ultra | 5x or 10x Pro |
| Agent curiosity, in a Muse country | Meta Muse free | Power if it fits | Limited testing, no published free cap |

## Common mistakes

1. **Paying for a "student code".** Anthropic's help center says it has no standing discounts available upon request and no standard discounted pricing for Pro, Max or Ultra. Be wary of third-party code sellers.
2. **Assuming a .edu email unlocks Pro.** Sign-in with a university email only helps when the school has a Claude agreement.
3. **Counting messages.** There is no published message count on any Claude plan. Anthropic says so directly.
4. **Mixing up Pro and the API.** Pro and Max do not include Console API usage. API credits are separate, except the monthly credits that come with Max and Ultra.
5. **Treating old videos as current.** Plan names and multipliers change. Anthropic's pricing page today lists Max at 5x Pro usage and Ultra at 10x weekly. Check claude.com/pricing.
6. **Ignoring renewal terms on promotions.** The scientists plan seats renew at the then-current price after 12 months.
7. **Putting student data into a plain account.** For teachers, Anthropic says identifiable student data requires authorization from the school or district.

## Checklist before you choose a plan

- Open claude.com/pricing and note today's price and any promotion.
- Use Free for a full week of real work and watch Settings > Usage.
- Write down whether you hit a limit, which tool triggered it, and when.
- If you are a teacher, student or lab member, check the free routes above before paying.
- If you need Claude Code or Research, go straight to Pro.
- Anthropic's pricing page says Pro is billed monthly or annually, so check the refund terms before you pay for a year.
- Re-check limits quarterly. Anthropic says it may adjust them to manage capacity.

## How we evaluated

**Sources.** Anthropic's pricing page, Pro plan and usage-limit help articles, Claude for Teachers announcement and program page, Claude for Education announcement and help article, the scientists plan help page and program terms, plus OpenAI's Free Tier FAQ, Go and Plus help pages, Google's Gemini subscriptions page and usage-limits help page, and Meta's Muse subscription help page. We fetched them on November 25, 2026, and checked every link.

**What we did.** Read and compared pages, verified a YouTube video through oEmbed, verified three X posts (all from @claudeai) through the syndication endpoint, confirmed four official images with HTTP 200 and image content types, confirmed every catalog and blog link returns 200, and confirmed the hosted skill download returns a zip.

**What we did not do.** We did not run Claude, ChatGPT, Gemini or Muse side by side. We did not measure how many messages Free allows, and we did not install or run any of the skills listed. We did not watch the embedded video end to end; we relied on its oEmbed title and channel.

**Where sources disagree.** Anthropic's pricing page lists a weekly limit for Free, while its Get started help article describes only a five-hour session limit. Anthropic's pricing page lists Pro at $17 per month annual, while the Pro help article gives $20. We report both. The custom-connector detail for Free comes from a third-party guide, and we flag it where used.

## FAQ

### Is Claude free to use?

Yes. The Free plan costs $0 and needs only an email address. It includes web search, file creation and code execution, memory, connectors, Artifacts, voice mode, up to five projects and Claude Design, Slides and Docs, with Sonnet and Haiku models. It has limited usage every five hours and every week, and no Opus, Fable or Claude Code.

### Is there a Claude free trial?

Not a standing one. Anthropic's help center says it occasionally runs limited-time promotions announced through official channels, and has no standing discounts on request. The Free plan is how you try Claude before paying.

### What is the difference between Claude Free and Claude Pro?

Pro adds more usage (at least 5x Free per 5-hour session per Anthropic), Opus, Claude Code, Research, hand-off and scheduled tasks, unlimited projects, Claude in Chrome, Claude for Microsoft 365 and usage credits. Pro costs $17 per month billed annually or $20 monthly as of November 25, 2026.

### How many messages do I get on Claude Free?

Anthropic does not publish a number. The pricing page says there is no fixed message count, and the help center says it varies with demand, message length, model and features. Any site quoting a precise daily number is guessing.

### Is Claude free for students?

The Free plan is free for everyone, students included. A university-sponsored Claude for Education account may cost you nothing if your school has signed a deal, and it adds higher limits, Projects and priority access. Anthropic offers no student discount on Pro, Max or Ultra.

### Is Claude free for teachers?

For verified K-12 educators in the US, yes. Claude for Teachers is free through July 30, 2028 (extended on November 13, 2026) and includes teaching skills, curriculum connectors, Claude Code and Cowork. It is not available outside the US, and it is not for university faculty.

### Can graduate students and researchers get Claude free?

Possibly. The Claude Team plan for scientists gives verified principal investigators at accredited universities and nonprofit institutes Standard seats at $0 for 12 months for their group (1 to 25 seats), with Premium seats at $15 per month. Availability is limited and the PI applies, not the student.

### Does Claude Free support skills and connectors?

Anthropic's pricing table marks both Skills and Connectors as Yes on Free. A third-party guide adds that skills need code execution on and that Free allows one custom connector. Plugins that bundle skills and connectors are, per the same guide, paid-only.

### Is Claude Free better than ChatGPT Free or Gemini free?

It depends on the job. Claude Free is strongest for documents, files and skills. OpenAI says ChatGPT Free has unlimited everyday text chats with separate tool caps and ads in some countries. Gemini free adds Deep Research, image generation and 15 GB of storage but throttles heavy features at peak demand. Test all three on your own work.

### Is Meta's Muse free?

Meta's help center says Muse is available for free with a usage limit, with Power at $20 per month and Maximum at $100 per month for more usage. It is in limited testing and not available in all locations.

### Does Claude Pro include API access?

No. Anthropic's Pro help article says the Pro plan does not include API usage through the Claude Console. Max and Ultra include monthly API credits ($100 and $200), and the Team plan for scientists includes pooled credits.

### Why does "cloud ai free" show Google Cloud and AWS results?

Because "cloud AI" also means AI services on cloud platforms. We searched the phrase on November 25, 2026 and the top results were Google Cloud and AWS free tiers and free-API lists, not Claude. If you meant the chatbot, the answer is here. If you meant developer APIs, use the vendors' own free-tier pages.

### Can I use Claude in Spanish for free?

The Free plan is open to anyone in a supported location, and Anthropic has a help article on using Claude in your preferred language. So the answer to "cloud ia gratis" is yes, there is a free plan. We have not tested Spanish quality, and we plan a Spanish version of this guide.

